"""Apply the Edukasaun LightDM login settings. Runs as root via pkexec.

LightDM has two Edukasaun-styled greeters, configured together so both look
and behave the same as the SDDM login screen:
  slick-greeter        /etc/lightdm/slick-greeter.conf ([Greeter])
  lightdm-gtk-greeter  /etc/xdg/lightdm/lightdm-gtk-greeter.conf.d/90-eduka-settings.conf
and the colors of the login card for the greeter's GTK theme
(Edukasaun-Login) in the lightdm account: ~lightdm/.config/gtk-3.0/gtk.css.

Reads one JSON object from standard input (written by Eduka-Settings).
The first argument picks what is changed, and with it the polkit action:
  --look             style, accent, clock, background, logo (and a small
                     copy of the logo for slick-greeter, made by Eduka-Settings)
                     (org.edukasaun.desktop.lightdm-config; administrators at
                     the computer need no password)
  --seat             greeter, hide the account list, typing a name, guest
                     (org.edukasaun.desktop.lightdm-login)
  --autologin        autologin_user ('' = off) (org.edukasaun.desktop.lightdm-autologin,
                     always asks for the password)
  --display-manager  display_manager: sddm | lightdm, used at the next start
                     (org.edukasaun.desktop.display-manager, always asks)

Every value is validated; pictures must be real PNG/JPEG/WebP/BMP files the
calling user may read, so this helper cannot be used to copy other files.
"""
import json, os, pwd, re, shutil, stat, subprocess, sys, tempfile

